^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "Bring several partially-implemented Spw parser/runtime concepts (n-range, label differentials, range-address/span-transform, indexing configurability) to full roundness, and retire the S0-S2/E0-E2 shorthand in docs now that code already speaks effect.l0/l1/l2/l3. Net-new grammar (named params, multi-arm select, stream fold, new operator products, membrane+body AST promotion) is scoped OUT of this branch pending design decisions — see ^[open]."
 ~#taste: "correctness + naming consistency: close the gap between code (EffectGrade already renamed) and docs (still S0-S3/E0-E2), and between AST partial support (NRangeNode, BodyNode exist) and its documented-but-unimplemented neighbors (multi-arm fold marked 'conceptual' in form-ladders.ts:379)"
}

